WEBVTT

NOTE Web version: narration as subtitles. Timing follows the transcript panels.

00:06.900 --> 00:12.000
In the 1970s, a young Raúl returns to Chile
after earning his doctorate

00:12.000 --> 00:16.900
at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

00:17.100 --> 00:22.300
The excitement sparked by the recent theory
of plate tectonics opens an important field in Chile,

00:22.300 --> 00:27.700
where we realise that plates
are subducting beneath our country.

00:28.000 --> 00:36.300
In the 1970s, a young Raúl meets a young José Vicente,
who was exploring the virtues of using the computer in music:

00:38.400 --> 00:45.800
“We believe it will be so, since human
imagination and creativity have no limits,

00:45.800 --> 00:53.200
and as long as humankind exists, music will keep exerting
the same fascination and deep meaning

00:53.200 --> 01:00.300
it has had throughout history, whatever the means
musicians have used to express themselves.”
— José Vicente Asuar

01:02.800 --> 01:13.000
In the 1970s, a young Raúl did not hold an anthropocentric view
and saw in the earth sciences a possible composer,

01:13.200 --> 01:19.500
and he proposes to the young José Vicente using
his analogue computer to listen to a seismic cycle.
